meta {
  name: List where a review can be published in a tool
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/incident-review-destinations/:automationConnection_id/targets
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  automationConnection_id: 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  The places a connection can publish an incident review into, read from the tool when you ask: Notion databases, Linear projects or Confluence spaces (`target_noun`), each with its `id` and `name` — a readable `key` where it has one, and `personal` for a person’s own Confluence space — team spaces first, and `last_target`, the one its Postmortems setting writes to. `parents` says whether the tool keeps pages in a tree, so a review can go under a page. When the tool will not answer, `targets` is empty and `error` says why.

  Scope: `monitoring.read`
}
